                <pb facs="0641" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2840</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-10-03T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 3,
                                1918, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>284. Your 430 and 431, September 29. There are definite limiting facts which
                    govern your proposal to organize American-Slavic legion. It is certain that no
                    money additional to the balance of $6,000,000 fund, which balance, I understand,
                    now approximates $1,300,000, is or will be available for this purpose. “You must
                    therefore consider the consequences of what may follow when fund is exhausted.
                    The President wants you to know how much we admire the spirit and success with
                    which you have guided matters at Archangel, but has serious doubts about the
                    undertaking. Please consider the foregoing carefully before you go further and
                    report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
